@startuml SillycationTripStateDiagram
title Sillycation - Trip State Diagram
hide empty description

'Initial State
[*] --> PLANNED : Trip created

'Trip State
state PLANNED
state ACTIVE
state COMPLETED
state ARCHIVED

'Transition
PLANNED --> ACTIVE : activate()\n[currentDate >= startDate\nand participantCount >= 2]

ACTIVE --> COMPLETED : complete()\n[currentDate >= endDate\nand all Episodes are COMPLETED]

COMPLETED --> ARCHIVED : archive()

ARCHIVED --> [*]

'State Rules
note right of PLANNED
  Participant set may change.

  Users may submit join requests.

  The creator may approve or reject
  pending join requests.

  Episodes cannot be created,
  submitted, or voted on.
end note


note right of ACTIVE
  Participant set is locked.

  No new join requests or approvals
  are allowed.

  Participants may create
  and submit Episodes.

  Eligible participants may vote.
end note


note right of COMPLETED
  The game is finished.

  No participants, Episodes,
  or Votes may be added or modified.

  The final ranking is definitive.

  The Trip remains visible
  in completed-trip history.
end note


note right of ARCHIVED
  The Trip is read-only.

  It is removed from the default
  Trip list.

  It remains accessible through
  the archive/history view.
end note

'General Contraint
note bottom
  Only the Trip creator may explicitly
  perform lifecycle transitions.

  Backward transitions and
  skipped transitions are not allowed.
end note

@enduml